var e={slug:`sardinia`,year:2026,destination:`Sardinia`,destinationIt:`Sardegna`,region:`Sardinia, Italy`,event:{name:`TRUE Sardegna 2026`,dates:`September 28 - October 1, 2026`,start:`2026-09-28`,end:`2026-10-01`,location:`Costa Smeralda, Sardinia`},title:`Sardinia 2026: The Numbers Behind Italy's Fastest-Growing Luxury Destination`,shortTitle:`Sardinia Luxury Travel Report 2026`,subtitle:`A market report for luxury travel advisors and hoteliers`,publisher:`TRUE Sardegna`,published:`2026-09-30`,publishedLabel:`September 2026`,dataAsOf:`September 2026`,version:`1.0`,readingMinutes:12,seo:{title:`Sardinia Luxury Travel Market Report 2026 | TRUE`,description:`Sardinia is Italy's fastest-growing tourism region. Key 2025-2026 data for luxury travel advisors and hoteliers: markets, the American traveller, Costa Smeralda, the whole island. From TRUE Sardegna 2026.`,keywords:[`luxury travel Sardinia`,`Sardinia tourism statistics 2026`,`Costa Smeralda luxury travel`,`Sardinia luxury hotels`,`TRUE Sardegna`]},intro:[`In 2023, Sardinia was the only Italian region where tourism declined. In 2025, ISTAT ranked it first in Italy for tourism growth. This report explains the turnaround with official data: who is travelling to Sardinia, where on the island the growth is happening, and what the 2026 season shows about the future of luxury travel in Sardinia.`,`It was presented at TRUE Sardegna 2026, the luxury travel trade event held on the Costa Smeralda from September 28 to October 1, 2026.`],glance:{title:`Sardinia at a glance`,items:[{n:`21.9 million`,l:`nights in 2025, an all-time record (+15.9% on 2024, +34.2% on 2023)`},{n:`5 million+`,l:`arrivals in 2025, a first for the island`},{n:`56%`,l:`share of nights from international guests in 2025 (50% in 2023)`},{n:`No.1`,l:`Italian region for tourism growth in 2025 (ISTAT)`},{n:`+246%`,l:`American nights in 2025 compared with 2019`},{n:`+8.24%`,l:`tourism growth in the first half of 2026, vs +4.43% for Italy`},{n:`+11.4%`,l:`international guests in 2026 so far`},{n:`67.2%`,l:`summer 2026 occupancy, 2nd in Italy (national average 61.8%)`},{n:`May 21, 2026`,l:`first-ever direct flight between the US and Sardinia`}],sources:`Sources: Regione Sardegna; ISTAT via ANSA; Italian Ministry of Tourism.`},chapters:[{id:`from-last-to-first`,num:`01`,title:`From last to first: Sardinia's tourism growth, 2023-2025`,short:`From last to first`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`The turnaround is recent and fast. In 2023, Sardinia recorded 14.2 million nights according to ISTAT, down 3.4% on 2022: the only region in Italy to decline in a year when the country as a whole beat its pre-pandemic record.`},{type:`p`,text:`By 2025 the picture had reversed. The regional tourism observatory, which uses the same method year after year, counted 21.9 million nights and more than 5 million arrivals, with an average stay of 4.24 nights. That is +15.9% on 2024 and +34.2% on 2023. ISTAT's final 2025 figures placed Sardinia first in Italy for percentage growth in tourism flows, ahead of Sicily and Puglia.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`bars`,title:`Nights in Sardinia, 2023-2025`,printHeight:540,unit:`million nights`,note:`Regional tourism observatory series (like-for-like, short-term rentals included).`,data:[{label:`2023`,value:16.3,display:`16.3M`,muted:!0},{label:`2024`,value:18.9,display:`18.9M`},{label:`2025`,value:21.9,display:`21.9M`,highlight:!0}],caption:`2023 and 2024 values derived from the observatory's published growth rates (+34.2% and +15.9%) on the 2025 total of 21.9 million nights. ISTAT's 2023 figure (14.2 million) uses a narrower perimeter.`},{type:`h3`,text:`The international tipping point`,printBreakBefore:!0},{type:`p`,text:`Growth came overwhelmingly from abroad. International nights rose 21.5% in 2025 and about 50% in two years, while Italian nights grew by around 10%. For the first time, foreign visitors clearly outnumbered Italians, with 56% of nights against 44%.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`split`,title:`Share of nights, 2025`,data:[{label:`International guests`,value:56,display:`56%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Italian guests`,value:44,display:`44%`}],caption:`In 2023 the split was 50/50.`},{type:`note`,title:`A note on the numbers`,text:`ISTAT began counting short-term rentals only in 2025, which inflates its year-on-year growth for Sardinia (+39% in nights). The regional observatory has always included them, so its +15.9% is the like-for-like figure, and the one used throughout this report.`}],sources:[{label:`ISTAT, tourism flows 2023 (via ANSA)`,key:`istat-2023`},{label:`Regione Sardegna, 2025 results (July 2026)`,key:`ras-2025`},{label:`ISTAT, tourism flows 2025 (via ANSA)`,key:`istat-2025`}]},{id:`who-is-travelling`,num:`02`,title:`Who is travelling to Sardinia`,short:`Who is travelling`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Germany, France and Switzerland are the backbone of Sardinian tourism, and all three set records in 2025.`},{type:`table`,title:`Top international markets, 2025`,columns:[`Market`,`Nights 2025`,`vs 2024`,`Note`],align:[`l`,`r`,`r`,`l`],rows:[[`Germany`,`3.26M`,`+19.8%`,`No.1 market, first time above 3 million; stays average 4.8 nights`],[`France`,`1.6M`,`+21.6%`,`French nights have more than tripled in ten years`],[`Switzerland`,`1.04M`,`-`,`Above 1 million nights for the first time`],[`United States`,`400,860`,`+34%`,`First market outside Europe`],[`Canada`,`116,000`,`+31%`,`Fastest long-haul growth since 2019`]]},{type:`p`,text:`The fastest growth comes from long-haul markets. Compared with 2019, Canada is up 263%, the United States 246%, Australia 166%, New Zealand 158% and India 120%, while China is still 16% below pre-pandemic levels. For luxury travel advisors this matters because long-haul travellers stay longer, book through advisors and travel outside the Italian peak weeks.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`hbars`,title:`Long-haul markets: nights in 2025 vs 2019`,unit:`% change`,data:[{label:`Canada`,value:263,display:`+263%`},{label:`United States`,value:246,display:`+246%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Australia`,value:166,display:`+166%`},{label:`New Zealand`,value:158,display:`+158%`},{label:`India`,value:120,display:`+120%`},{label:`China`,value:-16,display:`-16%`,muted:!0}]}],sources:[{label:`Regione Sardegna, July 2026`,key:`ras-2025`},{label:`Regione Sardegna data at BIT 2026, elaborated by Cipnes Gallura / UniOlbia`,key:`bit-2026`}]},{id:`american-traveller`,num:`03`,title:`The American luxury traveller in Sardinia`,short:`The American traveller`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`American travellers are still a small share of Sardinia's total, but no market has grown faster or matters more at the luxury end. In 2025, Sardinia welcomed 121,118 American visitors, who spent 400,860 nights on the island. About half of those nights are spent in Gallura, home of the Costa Smeralda, and US nights there doubled in two years.`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`121,118`,l:`American visitors in 2025`},{n:`400,860`,l:`American nights in 2025 (+34% on 2024)`},{n:`€80.05`,l:`highest average card payment of any nationality, first half of 2026`},{n:`+26%`,l:`US passengers arriving in Olbia by private jet in 2025 (to November)`}]},{type:`list`,items:[`American visitors make the highest average card payment of any nationality in Sardinia: €80.05 in the first half of 2026.`,`US passengers arriving in Olbia by private jet rose 26% in 2025 (to November) compared with 2024.`,`In a 2025 study of superyachts in Gallura, US owners were the largest single group: 72 of the 347 identified superyachts.`]},{type:`h3`,text:`Direct flights between New York and Sardinia`},{type:`p`,text:`On May 21, 2026, Delta launched the first-ever non-stop route between the US and Sardinia, New York JFK to Olbia, four times a week through October. The route carried about 2,700 passengers in its first weeks, with strong demand in business and premium cabins. United adds Newark-Olbia from May 27, 2027, three times a week. From 2027, northern Sardinia will have seven weekly flights to the New York area.`},{type:`timeline`,items:[{date:`May 21, 2026`,title:`Delta: New York JFK - Olbia`,text:`First-ever non-stop US-Sardinia route, four weekly flights through October.`},{date:`May 27, 2027`,title:`United: Newark - Olbia`,text:`Three weekly flights. Seven weekly flights to the New York area from 2027.`}]}],sources:[{label:`Regione Sardegna`,key:`ras-2025`},{label:`Sardegna Press, May 2026`,key:`delta-launch`},{label:`La Nuova Sardegna, Feb 2026`,key:`bit-2026`},{label:`TTG Italia`,key:`united-route`},{label:`olbia.it, June 2026`,key:`olbia-delta`},{label:`Gallura Oggi, Aug 2026`,key:`geasar-2026`}]},{id:`costa-smeralda-and-beyond`,num:`04`,title:`Luxury travel in Sardinia: the Costa Smeralda and beyond`,short:`Costa Smeralda and beyond`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Luxury tourism is a small slice of volume and a large slice of value. Across Italy, an Altagamma analysis found that 5-star and 5-star luxury hotels account for 1% of hotel businesses and 3% of hotel nights, but generate 25% of tourist spending; their guests spend nine times more than the average visitor.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`hbars`,title:`Five-star hotels in Italy: share of the total`,unit:`%`,max:100,data:[{label:`Hotel businesses`,value:1,display:`1%`,muted:!0},{label:`Hotel nights`,value:3,display:`3%`,muted:!0},{label:`Tourist spending`,value:25,display:`25%`,highlight:!0}],caption:`Altagamma analysis. Five-star guests spend nine times more than the average visitor.`},{type:`p`,text:`The Costa Smeralda is the heart of luxury travel in Sardinia. Gallura holds about 60% of the island's top-tier hotels, and Arzachena, the Costa Smeralda's municipality, ranks first in Sardinia for tourism value despite recording fewer nights than Alghero, with the highest average short-rental revenue at $51,250 per listing a year.`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`Luxury real estate`,text:`Porto Cervo holds Italy's record villa value, at up to €70,000 per square metre. It averages €11,575 per m² and, in the villa segment, now tops Portofino at around €21,000 per m².`},{title:`Private aviation`,text:`Olbia Costa Smeralda airport handled about 15,000 private aviation movements in 2024 (+10%), with more than 220 on peak days. Its operators report that private jet clients increasingly travel beyond the Costa Smeralda to the rest of the island.`},{title:`Yachting`,text:`2,330 yachts and superyachts visited the Costa Smeralda area in summer 2023, 30% more than in 2018. A 90-metre superyacht spends around €40,300 a day on shore.`},{title:`New luxury hotels in 2026`,text:`W Hotels on the Costa Smeralda and a 5-star luxury NH Collection in Cagliari, part of a national pipeline of 167 luxury openings expected in Italy by 2029.`}]}],sources:[{label:`Altagamma via Cipnes Gallura`,key:`altagamma`},{label:`Sardegna Press, June 2026`,key:`arzachena-value`},{label:`Il Sole 24 Ore, Aug 2026`,key:`porto-cervo`},{label:`La Nuova Sardegna (Geasar / Eccelsa)`,key:`private-aviation`},{label:`Cipnes / UniOlbia`,key:`yachting`},{label:`Forbes Italia`,key:`luxury-openings`},{label:`JLC News`,key:`luxury-openings`}]},{id:`growth-across-the-island`,num:`05`,title:`Growth across the whole island`,short:`Across the island`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Every Sardinian province grew in 2025. The fastest percentage growth came from Ogliastra on the east coast and the Sulcis in the southwest, areas known for nature, archaeology and food.`},{type:`map`,title:`Nights 2025 by area and growth on 2024`,areas:[{id:`gallura`,name:`Gallura`,nights:`7.7M`,value:7.7,growth:`+11.5%`,vs2023:`+34.6%`,lng:9.35,lat:40.95},{id:`cagliari`,name:`Cagliari metropolitan area`,nights:`5.17M`,value:5.17,growth:`+16.4%`,vs2023:`+34.0%`,lng:9.12,lat:39.3},{id:`sassari`,name:`Sassari metropolitan area`,nights:`3.30M`,value:3.3,growth:`+16.3%`,vs2023:`+34.7%`,lng:8.45,lat:40.65},{id:`ogliastra`,name:`Ogliastra`,nights:`1.77M`,value:1.77,growth:`+28.0%`,vs2023:`+42.9%`,lng:9.6,lat:39.95},{id:`sulcis`,name:`Sulcis`,nights:`687,000`,value:.687,growth:`+18.5%`,vs2023:`+50.3%`,lng:8.55,lat:39.2}]},{type:`p`,text:`Six towns now pass one million nights a year: Alghero (1.8 million, the most visited town on the island), Arzachena (about 1.4 million), Olbia (about 1.2 million), Cagliari, Orosei and San Teodoro.`},{type:`h3`,text:`A longer season`},{type:`p`,text:`A third of all nights now fall in April, May, September and October. Mid-season nights grew 39.2% compared with 2023, and winter nights 32.1%, although winter is still only 4% of the total. International guests drive the shoulder months: in 2023 they accounted for 71% of nights in May and 75% in October, and September had already overtaken June as the third busiest month.`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`1/3`,l:`of all nights fall in April, May, September and October`},{n:`+39.2%`,l:`mid-season nights compared with 2023`},{n:`71% / 75%`,l:`international share of nights in May and October (2023)`}]}],sources:[{label:`Regione Sardegna / ISTAT, July 2026`,key:`ras-2025`},{label:`Sardegna Press, June 2026`,key:`arzachena-value`},{label:`Cipnes / UniOlbia`,key:`bit-2026`}]},{id:`sardinia-in-2026`,num:`06`,title:`Sardinia in 2026: a record year, and then more`,short:`Sardinia in 2026`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Full-year 2026 figures will only be published next summer, but every indicator available so far points upward.`},{type:`table`,title:`Sardinia vs Italy, 2026`,columns:[`Indicator`,`Sardinia`,`Italy`],align:[`l`,`r`,`r`],rows:[[`Tourism growth, Jan-Jun 2026`,`+8.24%`,`+4.43%`],[`Summer 2026 occupancy`,`67.2% (2nd in Italy)`,`61.8%`]]},{type:`chart`,kind:`compare`,title:`Tourism growth, January-June 2026`,unit:`%`,data:[{label:`Sardinia`,value:8.24,display:`+8.24%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Italy`,value:4.43,display:`+4.43%`,muted:!0}]},{type:`list`,items:[`International guests: +11.4% in 2026 so far, against +4% for Italian guests.`,`Summer occupancy: up 13% on summer 2025.`,`Foreign air passengers: +19.3% compared with 2025 and +36.9% compared with 2024, from about 1.22 million in the first half of 2024 to about 1.67 million in the first half of 2026.`,`Every airport growing: in July 2026, Alghero +18.5%, Cagliari +10.2%, Olbia +8.7%. International passengers grew even faster: Alghero +53.4%, Cagliari +17%, Olbia +15.7%.`,`August: almost 1.3 million arrivals by air and sea in the first 28 days, level with 2025's record.`,`Autumn: nights booked for September were up 16.2% on 2025, and for October up 7.9%.`]},{type:`chart`,kind:`bars`,title:`Foreign passengers at Sardinian airports, January-June`,unit:`million passengers`,data:[{label:`2024`,value:1.22,display:`~1.22M`,muted:!0},{label:`2025`,value:1.4,display:`~1.40M`},{label:`2026`,value:1.67,display:`~1.67M`,highlight:!0}],caption:`+19.3% on the first half of 2025 and +36.9% on the first half of 2024.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`hbars`,title:`Airport passengers, July 2026 vs July 2025`,unit:`% change`,data:[{label:`Alghero, international`,value:53.4,display:`+53.4%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Alghero, total`,value:18.5,display:`+18.5%`},{label:`Cagliari, international`,value:17,display:`+17%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Cagliari, total`,value:10.2,display:`+10.2%`},{label:`Olbia, international`,value:15.7,display:`+15.7%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Olbia, total`,value:8.7,display:`+8.7%`}]}],sources:[{label:`Regione Sardegna / Viminale Alloggiati Web, July 2026`,key:`ras-h1-2026`},{label:`Italian Ministry of Tourism, Sept 2026`,key:`mitur-summer-2026`},{label:`Assaeroporti, foreign passengers January-June 2024-2026`,key:`assaeroporti-h1-2026`},{label:`Assaeroporti via Sassari Notizie, Sept 2026`,key:`assaeroporti-2026`},{label:`L'Unione Sarda, Aug 2026`,key:`unione-august-2026`}],sourcesNote:`September and October figures are bookings as of late August.`},{id:`beyond-the-beach`,num:`07`,title:`Beyond the beach: culture, longevity and slow luxury`,short:`Beyond the beach`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Sardinia's growth outside the peak months and outside the famous coastline rests on assets most international travellers have not yet discovered. They are also the stories that justify a longer, higher-value itinerary.`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`UNESCO heritage`,text:`In July 2025, UNESCO inscribed the domus de janas, prehistoric rock-cut tombs known as "fairy houses", as Italy's 61st World Heritage Site: 17 sites from Montessu in the Sulcis to Anghelu Ruju near Alghero, out of about 3,500 across the island. They join the Su Nuraxi nuraghe at Barumini, listed in 1997.`},{title:`Longevity`,text:`The villages of Barbagia and Ogliastra form the world's first identified Blue Zone. In Perdasdefogu, centenarians are 13 times more common than the Italian average, and men and women reach 100 in equal numbers.`},{title:`Recognition`,text:`Lonely Planet named Sardinia in its Best in Travel 2026 list, the only European destination included.`}]},{type:`p`,text:`These are the experiences that make Sardinia a destination for May, June, September and October, when most of the island's visitors are international.`}],sources:[{label:`Ministero della Cultura`,key:`unesco-domus`},{label:`UNESCO Italy`,key:`unesco-domus`},{label:`Musei Nazionali Sardegna`,key:`unesco-domus`},{label:`BlueZoneNews`,key:`blue-zone`},{label:`La Nuova Sardegna, Feb 2026`,key:`lonely-planet`}]},{id:`what-to-watch`,num:`08`,title:`What to watch, and what it means for the trade`,short:`What to watch`,blocks:[{type:`h3`,text:`Watch points`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`Summer concentration`,text:`CNA Sardegna warns that international demand is increasingly concentrating in the summer months, the same weeks Italians choose. That raises exposure to price pressure, capacity limits and external shocks. At Olbia, 68% of 2025 traffic fell between June and September.`},{title:`Value per visitor`,text:`Arrivals are rising, but in summer 2026 Confesercenti and Confcommercio reported spending in bars, restaurants and tourist services down 20-25%, with travellers more price-conscious. Growth in volume does not automatically mean growth in value.`},{title:`Infrastructure`,text:`Peak-season congestion is a recurring issue, from airport security lines in Cagliari to traffic on the Costa Smeralda.`}]},{type:`h3`,text:`What it means for advisors and hoteliers`},{type:`takeaways`,items:[{title:`Sell the shoulder months.`,text:`May, June, September and October deliver the island at its best, with better availability and an international crowd.`},{title:`Look beyond the Costa Smeralda.`,text:`Ogliastra, the Sulcis, the interior and Alghero are growing fastest and offer the heritage and food stories long-haul clients want.`},{title:`Build for the American client.`,text:`With seven weekly New York flights from 2027, US demand will keep rising. Premium cabins filled first in 2026.`},{title:`Book peak weeks early.`,text:`With occupancy at 67% across the summer and top properties near capacity, early commitments protect the best inventory.`}]}],sources:[{label:`CNA Sardegna, April 2026`,key:`cna-2026`},{label:`Gallura Oggi (Geasar data), Aug 2026`,key:`geasar-2026`},{label:`L'Agenzia di Viaggi Magazine / L'Unione Sarda, Aug 2026`,key:`spending-2026`}]}],faq:{destination:[{q:`Is Sardinia a luxury travel destination?`,a:`Yes. Sardinia, and the Costa Smeralda in particular, is one of Italy's leading luxury destinations. It has the country's highest villa prices in Porto Cervo, a concentration of five-star hotels in Gallura, one of Europe's busiest private aviation airports in summer, and a major superyacht scene.`},{q:`Is tourism in Sardinia growing?`,a:`Yes. ISTAT ranked Sardinia first in Italy for tourism growth in 2025, with a record 21.9 million nights. In the first half of 2026, tourism grew a further 8.24%, almost twice the national rate.`},{q:`Is there a direct flight from the US to Sardinia?`,a:`Yes. Since May 21, 2026, Delta has flown non-stop from New York JFK to Olbia. United will add Newark-Olbia from May 27, 2027.`},{q:`When is the best time for luxury travel to Sardinia?`,a:`May, June, September and October offer warm weather, fewer crowds and the island's international atmosphere. In 2026, nights booked for September were up 16.2% on 2025.`}],true:[{q:`What is TRUE?`,a:`TRUE is Italy's leading luxury travel network and B2B event platform. It connects over 5,000 luxury travel advisors worldwide with more than 300 hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs in Italy through immersive regional events that combine one-to-one meetings with fam trips.`},{q:`What is TRUE Sardegna?`,a:`TRUE Sardegna is the Sardinian edition of TRUE. It brings selected international travel advisors to meet Sardinia's luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs through B2B meetings, fam trips and immersive experiences. The 2026 edition took place from September 28 to October 1 on the Costa Smeralda.`},{q:`What are the best luxury travel networking events in Italy?`,a:`TRUE runs regional luxury travel trade events in Puglia, Sicily, the Dolomites and Sardinia, with Campania and Tuscany from 2027. Each edition brings selected international travel advisors together with the region's luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs.`},{q:`How is TRUE different from a traditional travel trade show?`,a:`TRUE combines one-to-one B2B appointments with fam trips, site inspections and destination experiences. Each edition features only suppliers from the host region, and participation is all-inclusive.`},{q:`Can travel advisors join a fam trip to Italy with TRUE?`,a:`Yes. Luxury travel advisors can apply to attend a TRUE edition. Selected advisors take part in an all-inclusive program of B2B meetings, fam trips and experiences in the host region.`},{q:`How can travel advisors or hotels take part in TRUE?`,a:`Travel advisors can apply to attend a TRUE edition, and luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs can join as exhibitors, through the TRUE application's forms.`}]},about:{title:`About TRUE: Italy's leading luxury travel network`,intro:`TRUE is Italy's leading luxury travel network and B2B event platform, connecting over 5,000 luxury travel advisors worldwide with more than 300 hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs across Italy. Founded in 2022 by Luigi De Santis, TRUE has quickly become a reference point for luxury travel networking between Italian hospitality and the world's top travel advisors, especially from the United States, Latin America and Australia.`,how:{title:`How TRUE works`,text:`Each TRUE event is dedicated to one Italian region and features only hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs from that region. Instead of a traditional trade show, TRUE uses an immersive format. Advisors meet exhibitors in pre-scheduled one-to-one B2B appointments, then experience the destination through fam trips, site inspections and curated experiences. Advisors come home knowing the product first-hand, and hotels meet buyers who are ready to sell. Participation is all-inclusive for both exhibitors and advisors, covering accommodation, B2B meetings, meals, transfers and events.`},network:{title:`A growing network`,intro:`Since 2022, TRUE has grown from a single event into a series of regional luxury travel events across Italy.`,items:[{title:`2026 editions`,text:`TRUE Puglia, TRUE Sicily, TRUE Dolomites and TRUE Sardegna.`},{title:`2027`,text:`TRUE Campania and TRUE Tuscany join the calendar.`},{title:`Selected advisors`,text:`Each year, hundreds of luxury travel advisors apply to attend TRUE, and about 180 top performers are selected, sent by the leading travel agencies and consortia in the US, Latin America and Australia.`},{title:`Road to TRUE`,text:`Once a year, TRUE takes about 60 Italian luxury hotels abroad to meet around 150 buyers in a key market such as New York.`},{title:`TRUEtalk`,text:`At every edition, a panel of hoteliers, buyers and journalists discusses the destination and the future of luxury travel.`}]},why:{title:`Why hotels and advisors choose TRUE`,items:[{title:`For hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs`,text:`Direct access to qualified luxury travel advisors from high-value long-haul markets, in a setting where they experience your property instead of just hearing about it.`,cta:`Apply as Exhibitor`,href:`https://hub.truevent.eu/exhibitor-application`},{title:`For travel advisors`,text:`An all-inclusive luxury fam trip in Italy combined with one-to-one meetings, destination training and relationships with the properties they sell.`,cta:`Apply as Buyer`,href:`https://hub.truevent.eu/buyer-application`}]}},sourceLinks:{"istat-2023":{label:`ISTAT, tourism flows in accommodation establishments 2023, via ANSA`,url:null},"istat-2025":{label:`ISTAT, tourism flows in accommodation establishments 2025, via ANSA and UniOlbia`,url:`https://www.ansa.it/sardegna/notizie/2026/07/23/turismo-con-219-milioni-di-presenze-la-sardegna-e-la-regione-che-cresce-di-piu_b83fb675-417e-4903-a06d-de11f6fb458b.html`},"ras-2025":{label:`Regione Autonoma della Sardegna, Assessorato del Turismo: 2025 results (July 2026)`,url:`https://www.regione.sardegna.it/notizie/turismo-in-sardegna-flussi-record-l-istat-certifica-che-la-sardegna`},"ras-h1-2026":{label:`Regione Autonoma della Sardegna: first-half 2026 data, Viminale Alloggiati Web (July 2026)`,url:`https://www.unionesarda.it/economia/turismo-da-record-nel-2026-la-conferma-dal-viminale-in-sardegna-8-24-di-arrivi-boom-di-stranieri-ho5bon7m`},"bit-2026":{label:`Regione Sardegna data presented at BIT 2026, elaborated by Cipnes Gallura / UniOlbia (La Nuova Sardegna, February 2026)`,url:`https://www.regione.sardegna.it/notizie/turismo-la-sardegna-in-vetrina-alla-bit-di-milano-anno-da-record-con-numer`},"delta-launch":{label:`Delta Air Lines, New York JFK - Olbia inaugural flight (Sardegna Press, May 2026)`,url:`https://www.shmag.it/sardegna/gallura/21_05_2026/new-york-olbia-atterrato-il-primo-volo-diretto-tra-stati-uniti-e-sardegna/`},"united-route":{label:`United Airlines, Newark - Olbia route announcement (TTG Italia)`,url:`https://www.teleregionelive.it/2026/08/25/olbia-united-airlines-apre-il-diretto-newark-olbia-tre-voli-a-settimana-dal-27-maggio-2027/`},"olbia-delta":{label:`olbia.it, first weeks of the Delta route (June 2026)`,url:`https://www.olbia.it/olbia-estate-record-allaeroporto-con-volo-diretto-per-new-york`},"geasar-2026":{label:`GEASAR / Olbia Costa Smeralda airport data (Gallura Oggi, August 2026)`,url:`https://www.galluraoggi.it/cronaca/united-airlines-olbia-volo-diretto-usa-25-agosto-2026/`},altagamma:{label:`Altagamma, luxury hospitality analysis, via Cipnes Gallura`,url:`https://www.cipnes.eu/news/turismo/costa-smeralda-e-turismo-di-lusso-tra-le-prime-5-aziende-della-sardegna`},"arzachena-value":{label:`Sardegna Press, tourism value by municipality (June 2026)`,url:`https://www.cipnes.eu/news/turismo/costa-smeralda-e-turismo-di-lusso-tra-le-prime-5-aziende-della-sardegna`},"porto-cervo":{label:`Il Sole 24 Ore, luxury real estate values (August 2026)`,url:`https://www.ilsole24ore.com/art/le-ville-piu-quotate-costiera-amalfitana-sardegna-e-toscana-58-milioni-vietri-mare-AJ4OZRw`},"private-aviation":{label:`La Nuova Sardegna, GEASAR / Eccelsa Aviation private aviation data`,url:null},yachting:{label:`Cipnes Gallura / UniOlbia, yachting and superyacht studies`,url:`https://www.cipnes.eu/news/nautica-/studio-arrivi-superyacht-in-gallura-2025`},"luxury-openings":{label:`Forbes Italia and JLC News, luxury hotel pipeline in Italy`,url:null},"mitur-summer-2026":{label:`Italian Ministry of Tourism, summer 2026 report (September 2026)`,url:`https://www.unionesarda.it/economia/estate-numeri-strabilianti-per-il-turismo-sardegna-al-top-svax7mtx`},"assaeroporti-2026":{label:`Assaeroporti, July 2026 traffic, via Sassari Notizie (September 2026)`,url:`https://www.sassarinotizie.com/2026/09/04/luglio-record-per-lo-scalo-di-alghero/`},"unione-august-2026":{label:`L'Unione Sarda, August 2026 arrivals and autumn bookings`,url:null},"unesco-domus":{label:`Ministero della Cultura, UNESCO Italy and Musei Nazionali Sardegna, domus de janas inscription (July 2025)`,url:`https://unesco.cultura.gov.it/news/le-domus-de-janas-sono-il-61-sito-italiano-nella-lista-del-patrimonio-mondiale/`},"blue-zone":{label:`BlueZoneNews, the Sardinian Blue Zone`,url:`https://www.tortohelie.it/notizie/sviluppo/ogliastra-terra-di-centenari-il-record-di-perdasdefogu/`},"lonely-planet":{label:`Lonely Planet, Best in Travel 2026`,url:`https://www.lonelyplanet.com/best-in-travel`},"cna-2026":{label:`CNA Sardegna, tourism seasonality report (April 2026)`,url:`https://cnasarda.it/media/RS_%20Turismo%20crescono%20incertezze%20e%20stagionalita.pdf`},"spending-2026":{label:`Confesercenti and Confcommercio, summer 2026 spending (L'Agenzia di Viaggi Magazine / L'Unione Sarda, August 2026)`,url:`https://www.unionesarda.it/news-sardegna/turisti-attenti-al-prezzo-e-scontrini-piu-bassi-la-ristorazione-in-sardegna-perde-il-20-wgkqovhq`},"assaeroporti-h1-2026":{label:`Assaeroporti, foreign passengers at Sardinian airports, January-June 2024-2026`,url:null}},sources:[`ISTAT, tourism flows in accommodation establishments (2023, 2025), via ANSA and UniOlbia`,`Regione Autonoma della Sardegna, Assessorato del Turismo: 2025 results and first-half 2026 data (July 2026)`,`Osservatorio del Turismo della Regione Sardegna; Viminale, Alloggiati Web platform`,`Italian Ministry of Tourism, summer 2026 report (September 2026)`,`Banca d'Italia; Assaeroporti; Sardegna Mobilità; GEASAR / Eccelsa Aviation`,`Delta Air Lines and United Airlines route announcements; TTG Italia; Gallura Oggi`,`Cipnes Gallura and UniOlbia; Altagamma; Il Sole 24 Ore; Abitare Co.; OMI data`,`Ministero della Cultura and UNESCO Italy; CNA Sardegna; Confesercenti and Confcommercio`],method:[{title:`Nights vs arrivals`,text:`"Nights" count each night spent in accommodation; "arrivals" count guests checking in. Growth rates are not interchangeable between the two.`},{title:`2026 data is provisional and partial`,text:`First-half figures come from the Alloggiati Web platform as analysed by the Region, and some sources describe the +8.24% as arrivals and others as nights. September and October figures are bookings, not final results.`},{title:`Older figures`,text:`Seasonality shares (2023), yacht arrivals (2023), private aviation (2024) and the Gallura five-star hotel share are the most recent published figures found and may since have changed.`}]},t={slug:`sicily`,year:2026,destination:`Sicily`,destinationIt:`Sicilia`,region:`Sicily, Italy`,event:{name:`TRUE Sicily 2026`,dates:`November 10-13, 2026`,start:`2026-11-10`,end:`2026-11-13`,location:`Verdura Resort, Sicily`},title:`Sicily 2026: The Numbers Behind the Growth of International Luxury Travel`,shortTitle:`Sicily Luxury Travel Report 2026`,subtitle:`A market report for luxury travel advisors and hoteliers`,publisher:`TRUE Sicily`,published:`2026-11-12`,publishAt:`2026-11-12T10:00:00+01:00`,publishedLabel:`November 2026`,dataAsOf:`October 2026`,version:`1.0`,readingMinutes:12,seo:{title:`Sicily Luxury Travel Market Report 2026 | TRUE`,description:`Sicily's tourism keeps growing, led by international and North American travellers. Key 2024-2026 data for luxury travel advisors and hoteliers: markets, hotel rates, Palermo, Taormina, Western Sicily. From TRUE Sicily 2026.`,keywords:[`luxury travel Sicily`,`Sicily tourism statistics 2026`,`Taormina luxury hotels`,`Western Sicily luxury travel`,`TRUE Sicily`]},intro:[`Sicily entered 2026 from an already high base, and its growth is now driven by international travellers, longer stays and rising hotel rates at the top of the market. This report brings together the latest available data: who is travelling to Sicily, the weight of North America, the performance of Palermo, Taormina and the southwest, and what it means for luxury travel advisors and hoteliers.`,`It was presented at TRUE Sicily 2026, the luxury travel trade event held at Verdura Resort from November 10 to 13, 2026.`],glance:{title:`Sicily at a glance`,items:[{n:`+18.4%`,l:`overnight stays, January-August 2026 compared with 2024*`},{n:`+4.9%`,l:`arrivals, January-August 2026 compared with 2024*`},{n:`+5.8%`,l:`overnight stays, January-August 2026 compared with 2025`},{n:`+8.5%`,l:`North American arrivals, first half of 2026 compared with 2025`},{n:`380K`,l:`US arrivals in 2024`},{n:`€1,500`,l:`leading Taormina five-star average daily rate`},{n:`+43%`,l:`luxury hotel average daily rate compared with 2019`},{n:`€1BN`,l:`real-estate investment in five years`},{n:`67%`,l:`share of investment capital from abroad`},{n:`2,500+`,l:`premium hotel rooms in the pipeline to 2030`},{n:`~46%`,l:`international share, Province of Agrigento`},{n:`+15.9%`,l:`US nights in Agrigento, 2025 compared with 2024`}],sources:`*Two-year compounded change from comparable January-August growth rates.`},chapters:[{id:`tourism-growth`,num:`01`,title:`Sicily's tourism growth, 2024-2026`,short:`Tourism growth`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Sicily entered 2026 from an already high base. In 2024 the regional series, including short-term rentals, recorded more than 22.4 million overnight stays. International travellers accounted for 12.05 million of them.`},{type:`p`,text:`Growth continued through 2025 and accelerated again in 2026. From January to August 2026, arrivals rose 3.6% and overnight stays 5.8% compared with the same period of 2025.`},{type:`p`,text:`On a comparable January-August basis, the compounded two-year change is about +18.4% in overnight stays and +4.9% in arrivals. Nights have grown around four times faster than arrivals: travellers are staying longer.`},{type:`chart`,kind:`compare`,title:`January-August 2026 compared with 2024`,unit:`%`,note:`Two-year compounded change from comparable January-August growth rates.`,data:[{label:`Overnight stays`,value:18.4,display:`+18.4%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Arrivals`,value:4.9,display:`+4.9%`,muted:!0}]},{type:`note`,title:`What it means for luxury travel`,text:`More nights per trip mean more room nights and more spending on restaurants, private transfers, guides, experiences, wine, shopping and additional destinations on the island.`}],sources:[{label:`Regione Siciliana / Osservatorio Turistico`,key:`osservatorio`},{label:`Regional Tourism Department, 2026`,key:`dipartimento-turismo`},{label:`UniCredit / Prometeia, 2026`,key:`unicredit`}]},{id:`international-demand`,printContinue:!0,num:`02`,title:`International demand is driving the market`,short:`International demand`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`12.05M`,l:`international overnight stays in 2024`},{n:`54%+`,l:`international share of nights entering 2026`}]},{type:`p`,text:`International travel has been one of the strongest drivers of Sicily's growth. Foreign travellers already generated 12.05 million nights in 2024, and by 2025 international demand had strengthened further while domestic demand softened.`},{type:`p`,text:`In the first half of 2026, North American arrivals rose 8.5% and French demand 4.2%. A larger international base supports five-star hotels, luxury resorts, villas, DMC services, private transfers and a broader shoulder season.`}],sources:[{label:`UniCredit / Prometeia, 2026`,key:`unicredit`},{label:`Assoimpresa Italia, 2026`,key:`assoimpresa`}]},{id:`north-america`,num:`03`,title:`North America: a luxury growth market`,short:`North America`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`379,829`,l:`American arrivals in 2024`},{n:`~1 million`,l:`American overnight stays in 2024`},{n:`+8.5%`,l:`US and Canadian arrivals, first half of 2026 compared with 2025`}]},{type:`p`,text:`The United States was Sicily's second-largest foreign market in 2024. In Taormina, American travellers generated about 262,000 hotel nights: 19% of all hotel nights and 22% of international hotel nights.`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`22%`,l:`US share of international hotel nights in Taormina`},{n:`~€1,500`,l:`average daily rate at Taormina's leading five-star hotels`}]},{type:`p`,text:`North American growth directly supports the products where Sicily's luxury market is expanding:`},{type:`list`,items:[`five-star hotels and resorts, suites and villas;`,`private transfers and private guides;`,`wine and gastronomy, yachts and celebration travel;`,`multi-stop itineraries across the island.`]}],sources:[{label:`Regione Siciliana`,key:`rapporto-2024`},{label:`ISTAT, tourism flows 2024`,key:`istat-2024`},{label:`Taormina market data`,key:`taormina`},{label:`HVS`,key:`hvs-taormina`},{label:`2026 North America growth data`,key:`assoimpresa`}]},{id:`roots-travel`,num:`04`,title:`Back to the roots travel`,short:`Roots travel`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`A growing number of international travellers are coming to Sicily to rediscover their family heritage, exploring the places, stories and traditions of their ancestors.`},{type:`stats`,large:!0,items:[{n:`~€5 billion`,l:`economic flow generated by roots tourism in Italy in 2024, +34.4% on 2023`},{n:`6.6M`,l:`roots travellers to Italy in 2024`},{n:`63.8%`,l:`of Palermo's overnight stays generated by international visitors in 2025, up from 60.4% in 2024`}]},{type:`h3`,text:`Same roots. New journeys.`}],sources:[{label:`Ministero degli Affari Esteri (MAECI), Turismo delle radici`,key:`maeci-radici`},{label:`Comune di Palermo / Osservatorio Turistico Regione Siciliana`,key:`palermo`}]},{id:`palermo`,num:`05`,title:`Palermo: international demand gains share`,short:`Palermo`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`2.1M`,l:`overnight stays in Palermo in 2025`},{n:`+13.4%`,l:`international nights, 2025 compared with 2024`},{n:`63.8%`,l:`international share of nights in 2025`}]},{type:`chart`,kind:`bars`,title:`Palermo: international share of nights`,unit:`% of nights`,data:[{label:`2019`,value:54.7,display:`54.7%`,muted:!0},{label:`2024`,value:60.4,display:`60.4%`},{label:`2025`,value:63.8,display:`63.8%`,highlight:!0}]},{type:`p`,text:`The largest increase by nationality in 2025, in absolute terms, came from the United States: +22,756 nights.`},{type:`p`,text:`For luxury travel, Palermo is both a high-end city destination and the gateway to Western Sicily: Cefalù, Monreale, Scopello, Trapani, Marsala and the Egadi Islands.`}],sources:[]},{id:`luxury-hotel-rates`,num:`06`,title:`Luxury hotel rates are outgrowing the market`,short:`Luxury hotel rates`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`+43%`,l:`luxury hotel average daily rate in Sicily compared with 2019`},{n:`>80%`,l:`real growth in Taormina's average daily rate since 2018`},{n:`~76%`,l:`hotel occupancy in Taormina, April-October`}]},{type:`p`,text:`Taormina's leading five-star hotels achieved average daily rates of about €1,500 in 2025. The increase has been driven mainly by rate rather than by a comparable rise in occupancy. At the luxury end, Sicily is growing through value per occupied room, not only through visitor numbers.`},{type:`h3`,text:`Investment and new luxury inventory`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`€1 billion`,l:`real-estate investment in five years`},{n:`46%`,l:`share directed to hotels`},{n:`67%`,l:`share of capital from abroad`}]},{type:`p`,text:`More than 2,500 premium hotel rooms are in the pipeline through 2030. New luxury openings bring global sales networks, international PR and access to high-value distribution.`}],sources:[{label:`HVS`,key:`hvs-taormina`},{label:`CBRE Italy`,key:`cbre`}]},{id:`southwestern-sicily`,printContinue:!0,tipografiaNewPage:!0,num:`07`,title:`Southwestern Sicily`,short:`Southwestern Sicily`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`1.73M`,l:`overnight stays in the Province of Agrigento in 2025`},{n:`~46%`,l:`international share of nights`},{n:`+15.9%`,l:`American nights, 2025 compared with 2024`}]},{type:`p`,text:`American overnight stays in the province reached 103,227 in 2025, with an average stay of 3.8 nights. The area brings together Verdura, Sciacca, Agrigento, Selinunte and Menfi, in a market where international travellers already generate half of all nights.`},{type:`p`,text:`The luxury opportunity is measurable: established resorts, major archaeology, wine and coastline can support longer stays and higher-value itineraries, while the area is still less internationally developed than Taormina or Palermo.`}],sources:[]},{id:`culture`,num:`08`,title:`Culture is generating scale`,short:`Culture`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`1M+`,l:`visitors to the Valley of the Temples, first half of 2026`}]},{type:`chart`,kind:`hbars`,title:`Visitors to archaeological parks, first half of 2026`,unit:`% change`,data:[{label:`Caltagirone archaeological park`,value:65,display:`+65%`,highlight:!0},{label:`Adrano`,value:19,display:`+19%`},{label:`Catania and Valle dell'Aci`,value:17,display:`+17%`},{label:`Villa Romana del Casale`,value:11,display:`+11%`}]},{type:`p`,text:`Archaeology, architecture and historic cities give travellers reasons to visit outside the summer, and provide the content for private guiding, specialist access and multi-stop itineraries. For the luxury segment, cultural assets can turn a resort stay into a longer journey across Sicily.`}],sources:[{label:`Regione Siciliana archaeological parks; Valley of the Temples data`,key:`parchi`}]},{id:`longer-season`,printContinue:!0,tipografiaNewPage:!0,num:`09`,title:`A longer season`,short:`A longer season`,blocks:[{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`65.6%`,l:`accommodation occupancy, summer 2026`},{n:`+12%`,l:`experience bookings, 2026 compared with 2025`}]},{type:`p`,text:`January and March 2026 each grew by about 7%, while overnight stays from January to August rose 5.8%. Summer demand remained high. The opportunity is to grow April to June and September to November through culture, wine, gastronomy, archaeology and golf.`},{type:`p`,text:`Longer stays and stronger demand for experiences increase the value of private guides, restaurants, wineries, boats, drivers, artisans and cultural access. Growth in nights and experiences matters more economically than growth in arrivals alone.`}],sources:[]},{id:`east-and-west`,num:`10`,title:`East and West: two complementary growth stories`,short:`East and West`,blocks:[{type:`p`,text:`Eastern and Western Sicily are not competing destinations. Their different levels of international recognition, hotel infrastructure and visitor distribution can help sell richer, longer itineraries across the whole island.`},{type:`h3`,text:`Eastern Sicily: the established luxury benchmark`},{type:`p`,text:`From Taormina and Mount Etna to Catania, Siracusa and the Val di Noto, Eastern Sicily combines international brand recognition, iconic cultural sites and a mature luxury hospitality offer.`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`3.99M`,l:`overnight stays in the Province of Messina in 2024`},{n:`+7.2%`,l:`Province of Messina, nights compared with 2023`},{n:`~22%`,l:`US share of international hotel nights in Taormina`}]},{type:`p`,text:`Taormina remains Sicily's most internationally established luxury destination. Heritage hotels, international hospitality brands, dramatic scenery and cultural programming have supported premium pricing, with leading five-star average daily rates approaching €1,500. These figures describe the top of the Taormina market, not an island-wide average.`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`Catania and Etna`,text:`Airport access, the volcanic landscape, wineries and outdoor experiences make a gateway for premium itineraries and shoulder-season demand.`},{title:`Siracusa and Ortigia`,text:`Archaeology, architecture, waterfront hospitality and private cultural experiences appeal strongly to experiential luxury travellers.`},{title:`Val di Noto`,text:`Noto, Modica and Ragusa bring UNESCO-listed Baroque heritage, design-led stays and a distinctive food identity.`}]},{type:`p`,text:`What comes next: Eastern Sicily's opportunity is to build on established demand while spreading tourism more widely across the region. Better connections between the major gateways, resorts and cultural destinations can encourage longer itineraries and reduce concentration in peak-season hotspots.`},{type:`h3`,text:`Western Sicily: a growing luxury destination`},{type:`p`,text:`Western and Southwestern Sicily bring together Agrigento, Sciacca, Menfi, Selinunte, Marsala, Trapani and Palermo. The area offers a complementary luxury proposition built on coastal resorts, archaeology, wineries and food, connected in an itinerary rather than centred on one resort town.`},{type:`stats`,items:[{n:`1.73M`,l:`overnight stays in the Province of Agrigento in 2025`},{n:`~46%`,l:`international share, Province of Agrigento, 2025`},{n:`+26.74%`,l:`nights in the Province of Agrigento, 2025 compared with 2019*`}]},{type:`p`,text:`Sciacca recorded 514,897 overnight stays in 2025. The Agrigento-Sciacca corridor links the Valley of the Temples with resort hospitality and the surrounding coastline, and US nights in the province rose 15.9% in 2025.`},{type:`p`,text:`Rocco Forte's Verdura Resort is an internationally recognised luxury anchor. Its golf, wellness, food and coastal setting support premium stays, and its location introduces guests to Agrigento, Selinunte and Menfi. The opportunity is to connect international resort demand with local guides, wineries, restaurants, transport and cultural experiences.`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`Selinunte and Menfi`,text:`Archaeology, vineyards and coastal experiences can extend resort-based stays.`},{title:`Marsala and Trapani`,text:`Wine heritage, historic towns, the salt pans and access to the Egadi Islands support varied itineraries.`},{title:`Palermo`,text:`A major international city gateway, cultural destination and complementary stop on a western itinerary.`}]},{type:`p`,text:`The development priority: the opportunity is to turn strong cultural interest and growing international demand into longer stays, higher local spending and more year-round employment. Destination access, consistent service quality and high-end experiences will be essential.`},{type:`h3`,text:`Comparable provincial snapshot, 2024`},{type:`table`,title:`Messina (East) and Trapani (West), 2024`,columns:[`Indicator`,`Messina / East`,`Trapani / West`],align:[`l`,`r`,`r`],rows:[[`Overnight stays`,`3,991,919`,`2,544,726`],[`Growth compared with 2023`,`+7.2%`,`+11.8%`],[`Reading`,`Larger established market`,`Faster growth in 2024`]]},{type:`note`,title:`A note on the comparison`,text:`These are province-level figures for a single year: they do not show that the whole western region is growing faster than the whole eastern region. Agrigento's 2025 figures are not directly comparable with these 2024 totals, and the 2019-2025 Agrigento growth excludes rental accommodation.`},{type:`h3`,text:`Distinct commercial advantages`},{type:`cards`,items:[{title:`Eastern Sicily`,text:`Globally recognised luxury gateways, high hotel pricing power, established international distribution, iconic cultural attractions and sophisticated resort infrastructure.`},{title:`Western Sicily`,text:`Established luxury anchors alongside emerging circuits, strong archaeological and coastal assets, meaningful international demand and opportunities to build higher-value multi-stop itineraries.`}]},{type:`h3`,text:`A strategic role for TRUE Sicily 2026`},{type:`p`,text:`The commercial goal is not simply to sell a second hotel, but more nights in Sicily. An itinerary linking Taormina, Etna and Siracusa with Agrigento, Sciacca and the western coast introduces new experiences, increases spending in the destination and gives returning clients a reason to explore further. Hosting TRUE at Verdura Resort showcases the southwest while keeping the whole island in view.`}],sources:[{label:`Regione Siciliana tourism reports`,key:`rapporto-2024`},{label:`HVS Taormina Market Pulse 2026`,key:`hvs-taormina`},{label:`Agrigento Chamber of Commerce`,key:`cciaa-agrigento`}],sourcesNote:`*2019-2025 Agrigento growth excludes rental accommodation. Messina is a provincial benchmark, not a complete Eastern Sicily total; Taormina hotel indicators refer to a narrower market.`},{id:`what-it-means`,num:`11`,title:`The numbers, and what they mean for the trade`,short:`What it means`,blocks:[{type:`table`,title:`The numbers behind Sicily's growth`,columns:[`Indicator`,`Period`,`Change`],align:[`l`,`l`,`r`],rows:[[`Overnight stays`,`Jan-Aug 2026 vs 2024*`,`+18.4%`],[`Arrivals`,`Jan-Aug 2026 vs 2024*`,`+4.9%`],[`North American arrivals`,`H1 2026 vs H1 2025`,`+8.5%`],[`Palermo, international nights`,`2025 vs 2024`,`+13.4%`],[`Agrigento, American nights`,`2025 vs 2024`,`+15.9%`],[`Luxury hotel average daily rate`,`Latest vs 2019`,`+43%`],[`Experience bookings`,`2026 vs 2025`,`+12%`]]},{type:`h3`,text:`What it means for advisors and hoteliers`},{type:`takeaways`,items:[{title:`Sell more nights, not only more arrivals.`,text:`Nights are growing much faster than arrivals, and Sicily has the product for longer stays across several destinations.`},{title:`Build for international demand.`,text:`Foreign travellers are the majority, and increasingly important outside the summer peak.`},{title:`Treat North America as a core luxury market.`,text:`Almost one million American nights in 2024, and North American demand is still growing.`},{title:`Follow the rate growth.`,text:`Luxury rates are 43% above 2019, and Taormina shows the spending power at the top of the market.`},{title:`Watch Southwestern Sicily.`,text:`About half of Agrigento's nights are international, and American nights are growing at double-digit rates.`},{title:`Sell the shoulder season.`,text:`Culture, wine, food and golf give Sicily the product to grow beyond July and August.`}]}],sources:[],sourcesNote:`*Two-year compounded change from comparable January-August growth rates.`}],faq:{destination:[{q:`Is Sicily a luxury travel destination?`,a:`Yes. Taormina's leading five-star hotels reach average daily rates of about €1,500, luxury hotel rates across Sicily are 43% above 2019, and more than 2,500 premium hotel rooms are in the pipeline to 2030. Palermo, Siracusa, the Val di Noto and the southwest around Verdura Resort complete the offer.`},{q:`Is tourism in Sicily growing?`,a:`Yes. From January to August 2026, overnight stays rose 5.8% and arrivals 3.6% compared with 2025, about +18.4% in nights compared with 2024. International travellers account for more than half of all nights.`},{q:`How important are American travellers to Sicily?`,a:`Very. The United States was Sicily's second-largest foreign market in 2024, with about 380,000 arrivals and almost one million nights. North American arrivals rose a further 8.5% in the first half of 2026.`},{q:`When is the best time for luxury travel to Sicily?`,a:`April to June and September to November combine pleasant weather with culture, wine, food, archaeology and golf, and fewer crowds than July and August. January and March 2026 each grew by about 7%, a sign that the season is getting longer.`}],true:[{q:`What is TRUE?`,a:`TRUE is Italy's leading luxury travel network and B2B event platform. It connects over 5,000 luxury travel advisors worldwide with more than 300 hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs in Italy through immersive regional events that combine one-to-one meetings with fam trips.`},{q:`What is TRUE Sicily?`,a:`TRUE Sicily is the Sicilian edition of TRUE. It brings selected international travel advisors to meet Sicily's luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs through B2B meetings, fam trips and immersive experiences. The 2026 edition took place at Verdura Resort in November 2026.`},{q:`What are the best luxury travel networking events in Italy?`,a:`TRUE runs regional luxury travel trade events in Puglia, Sicily, the Dolomites and Sardinia, with Campania and Tuscany from 2027. Each edition brings selected international travel advisors together with the region's luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs.`},{q:`How is TRUE different from a traditional travel trade show?`,a:`TRUE combines one-to-one B2B appointments with fam trips, site inspections and destination experiences. Each edition features only suppliers from the host region, and participation is all-inclusive.`},{q:`Can travel advisors join a fam trip to Italy with TRUE?`,a:`Yes. Luxury travel advisors can apply to attend a TRUE edition. Selected advisors take part in an all-inclusive program of B2B meetings, fam trips and experiences in the host region.`},{q:`How can travel advisors or hotels take part in TRUE?`,a:`Travel advisors can apply to attend a TRUE edition, and luxury hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs can join as exhibitors, through the TRUE application's forms.`}]},about:{title:`About TRUE: Italy's leading luxury travel network`,intro:`TRUE is Italy's leading luxury travel network and B2B event platform, connecting over 5,000 luxury travel advisors worldwide with more than 300 hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs across Italy. Founded in 2022 by Luigi De Santis, TRUE has quickly become a reference point for luxury travel networking between Italian hospitality and the world's top travel advisors, especially from the United States, Latin America and Australia.`,how:{title:`How TRUE works`,text:`Each TRUE event is dedicated to one Italian region and features only hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs from that region. Instead of a traditional trade show, TRUE uses an immersive format. Advisors meet exhibitors in pre-scheduled one-to-one B2B appointments, then experience the destination through fam trips, site inspections and curated experiences. Advisors come home knowing the product first-hand, and hotels meet buyers who are ready to sell. Participation is all-inclusive for both exhibitors and advisors, covering accommodation, B2B meetings, meals, transfers and events.`},network:{title:`A growing network`,intro:`Since 2022, TRUE has grown from a single event into a series of regional luxury travel events across Italy.`,items:[{title:`2026 editions`,text:`TRUE Puglia, TRUE Dolomites, TRUE Sardegna and TRUE Sicily.`},{title:`2027`,text:`TRUE Campania and TRUE Tuscany join the calendar.`},{title:`Selected advisors`,text:`Each year, hundreds of luxury travel advisors apply to attend TRUE, and about 180 top performers are selected, sent by the leading travel agencies and consortia in the US, Latin America and Australia.`},{title:`Road to TRUE`,text:`Once a year, TRUE takes about 60 Italian luxury hotels abroad to meet around 150 buyers in a key market such as New York.`},{title:`TRUEtalk`,text:`At every edition, a panel of hoteliers, buyers and journalists discusses the destination and the future of luxury travel.`}]},why:{title:`Why hotels and advisors choose TRUE`,items:[{title:`For hotels, resorts, villas and DMCs`,text:`Direct access to qualified luxury travel advisors from high-value long-haul markets, in a setting where they experience your property instead of just hearing about it.`,cta:`Apply as Exhibitor`,href:`https://hub.truevent.eu/exhibitor-application`},{title:`For travel advisors`,text:`An all-inclusive luxury fam trip in Italy combined with one-to-one meetings, destination training and relationships with the properties they sell.`,cta:`Apply as Buyer`,href:`https://hub.truevent.eu/buyer-application`}]}},sourceLinks:{"rapporto-2024":{label:`Regione Siciliana - Osservatorio Turistico: Il turismo in Sicilia, Rapporto 2024 (March 2026)`,url:`https://www.regione.sicilia.it/system/files/2026-03/rapporto_2024_0.pdf`},osservatorio:{label:`Regione Siciliana - Osservatorio Turistico: tourism movements, source markets and regional tourism reports`,url:`https://www.guidaviaggi.it/2025/10/09/incoming-la-sicilia-cresce-ancora-119-di-presenze/`},"dipartimento-turismo":{label:`Regione Siciliana - Dipartimento Turismo: 2025 and 2026 tourism performance and seasonality releases`,url:`https://www.palermotoday.it/economia/turismo-sicilia-palermo-arrivi-presenze-crescita-2026.html`},unicredit:{label:`UniCredit / Prometeia - Le nuove sfide del comparto turistico in Sicilia (March 2026)`,url:`https://www.unicreditgroup.eu/it/press-media/news/2026/march/le-nuove-sfide-del-comparto-turistico-in-sicilia-.html`},"istat-2024":{label:`ISTAT - I flussi turistici, anno 2024`,url:`https://www.istat.it/comunicato-stampa/i-flussi-turistici-anno-2024/`},"hvs-taormina":{label:`HVS - Taormina Market Pulse 2026: luxury average daily rate, occupancy and long-term rate performance`,url:`https://www.hvs.com/article/10377-taormina-market-pulse-2026-from-the-grand-tour-heritage-to-a-global-luxury-destination`},cbre:{label:`CBRE Italy - Sicilia on Stage: real-estate investment, foreign capital and premium hotel pipeline`,url:`https://www.cbre.it/insights/reports/sicilia-on-stage`},mitur:{label:`Ministero del Turismo: summer 2026 accommodation occupancy`,url:`https://www.guidaviaggi.it/2026/09/14/ministro-mazzi-estate-da-record-con-276-milioni-di-presenze/`},palermo:{label:`Comune di Palermo / local tourism statistics: city overnight stays and international share`,url:`https://www.comune.palermo.it/novita/dati-turismo-2025-palermo-supera-i-2-milioni-di-presenze-dichiarazione-sindaco-lagalla/`},parchi:{label:`Regione Siciliana archaeological parks / Valley of the Temples: cultural-site visitation`,url:`https://parchiarcheologici.regione.sicilia.it/en/blog/parchi-archeologici-siciliani-crescono-le-visite-la-valle-dei-templi-supera-il-milione-di-ingressi/`},assoimpresa:{label:`Assoimpresa Italia: 2026 North American and experiential-demand indicators`,url:`https://www.assoimpresaitalia.it/2026/09/16/turismo-stagione-da-record-piano-destagionalizzazione/`},taormina:{label:`Taormina market data`,url:`https://messina.gazzettadelsud.it/articoli/economia/2025/03/16/taormina-il-turismo-colleziona-grandi-numeri-opportunita-per-territorio-e-giovani-98a662f3-c8a5-481e-a830-316c8f0652d6/`},"cciaa-agrigento":{label:`Agrigento Chamber of Commerce`,url:`https://www.agrigentonotizie.it/economia/turismo-presenze-crescita-pernottamenti-camera-commercio-2025.html`},"maeci-radici":{label:`Ministero degli Affari Esteri e della Cooperazione Internazionale (MAECI) - Turismo delle radici: roots travellers and economic flow 2024`,url:`https://www.esteri.it/it/servizi-opportunita/italiani-all-estero/turismo-delle-radici/`}},sources:[`Regione Siciliana - Osservatorio Turistico: tourism movements, source markets and regional tourism reports`,`Regione Siciliana - Dipartimento Turismo: 2025 and 2026 tourism performance and seasonality releases`,`HVS - Taormina Market Pulse 2026: luxury average daily rate, occupancy and long-term rate performance`,`CBRE Italy - Sicilia on Stage: real-estate investment, foreign capital and premium hotel pipeline`,`Ministero del Turismo: summer 2026 accommodation occupancy`,`Comune di Palermo / local tourism statistics: city overnight stays and international share`,`Regione Siciliana archaeological parks / Valley of the Temples: cultural-site visitation`,`Assoimpresa Italia: 2026 North American and experiential-demand indicators`,`Ministero degli Affari Esteri e della Cooperazione Internazionale (MAECI) - Turismo delle radici: roots travellers and economic flow 2024`],method:[{title:`2026 data is partial`,text:`2026 figures cover part of the year and should not be read as full-year results.`},{title:`Compounded two-year changes`,text:`The +18.4% in overnight stays and +4.9% in arrivals for January-August 2026 compared with 2024 are calculated by compounding comparable consecutive growth rates.`},{title:`Different perimeters`,text:`Definitive and provisional regional series, and provincial or city statistics, may use different accommodation perimeters, so they are not treated as interchangeable. Comparisons between East and West use only matching periods and are not a unified time series.`}]},n=!0,r=[e,t].filter(e=>n).sort((e,t)=>(t.published||``).localeCompare(e.published||``)),i=e=>`/reports/${e}`,a=e=>`/reports/${e.slug}/${e.year}`,o=e=>`TRUE-${e.destination.replace(/\s+/g,`-`)}-Report-${e.year}.pdf`,s=e=>`${a(e)}/${o(e)}`;function c(e,t){return r.find(n=>n.slug===e&&String(n.year)===String(t))||null}function l(e){return r.filter(t=>t.slug===e)}function u(){let e=new Map;for(let t of r)e.has(t.slug)||e.set(t.slug,{slug:t.slug,destination:t.destination,editions:[]}),e.get(t.slug).editions.push(t);return[...e.values()]}export{i as a,u as i,a as n,l as o,s as r,c as t};